<p>Note: The pro forma results reflect income taxes as if the company had been a C-corporation for all periods.  The 1997 pro forma results do not include the following first quarter adjustments; recording of related deferred tax liabilities, the one-time $20,290 million charge relating to termination of deferred compensation agreements with certain employees, $2,506 million charge relating to the early extinguishment of debt, and $1,491 million of interest expense as a result of reductions in indebtedness.  The 1996 pro forma results do not include $1,881 and $1,475 million of interest expense for the second and first quarter, respectively, as a result of reductions in indebtedness.  All charges relate to the termination of the company's S-corporation status and corporate reorganization in connection with its initial public offering on February 21, 1997.</p>
